      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Ah, the Eurostar, a swift and efficient way to travel from London to Paris, much like a well-trained goblin on a mission to deliver a precious artifact. As for your luggage, the Eurostar allows you to bring along a bag of treasures, but it must not exceed 32kg (70lbs) and should fit within the dimensions of 62cm (24.4in) x 32cm (12.6in) x 23cm (9.1in). Think of it as a goblin's satchel, not too heavy, but just enough to carry your essentials.\n\nNow, regarding the time you should allow for check-in and security at St Pancras, it's best to arrive like a goblin preparing for a grand feast; early is always wise. Aim to be there at least 2 hours before your train's departure. This will give you ample time to navigate the check-in process, pass through security, and perhaps even catch a glimpse of the bustling London Underground, much like a goblin observing the comings and goings of the city. Remember, punctuality is key, even for goblins!",
